<title>USA: CFTC disciplines Chicago broker Kevin Hanley.</title>
<headline>CFTC disciplines Chicago broker Kevin Hanley.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Commodity Futures Trading Commission said Kevin Hanley would be subject to conditional registration as a floor broker for two years because he pleaded guilty to misdemeanor theft.</p>
<p>Hanley pleaded guility in May 1995, more than a year before he received trading privileges at the Chicago Board of Trade.</p>
<p>In an announcement, CFTC said it and Hanley, of Glen Ellyn, Ill., had agreed to a plan in which Hanley would be closely supervised for two years. During that time, Hanley would not be allowed any management duties.</p>
</text>
